  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 304</b></color></size>

    <b>The stone chariot, Hampi</b>

    <size=74%>Early 16th century

    <i>Granite</i>

    In situ, Vittala Temple, Hampi, Karnataka (UNESCO World Heritage Site)</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    In the courtyard of the Vittala Temple stands a shrine for Garuda carved in the shape of a temple chariot. Hampi was Vijayanagara, capital of one of the largest empires in Indian history, which foreign visitors described as one of the richest cities in the world.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Ram Nagesh Thota / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
