  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 307</b></color></size>

    <b>Wine cup of Shah Jahan</b>

    <size=74%>1657

    <i>White nephrite jade</i>

    Victoria and Albert Museum, London</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Carved from a single piece of white jade, this cup is shaped like half a gourd, with a handle in the form of a wild goat''s head and a lotus base. An inscription records that it was made for Shah Jahan in 1657. It shows the Mughal love of carving hard stones.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Unknown / CC BY-SA 3.0 / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
